  "details": "So I tried the app with headphones, and I noticed huge audio issues.\n\nThe audio just sounds very low quality, the issue seems to happen if there are at least 2 audio sources playing at the same time. It kinda sounded like each audio source had noise cancellation enabled, and that each audio source was played thought a phone microphone first.\n\nBut the really weird thing is when I recorded the screen, and played back the video, the audio quality of the video was really great, and I didn't notice any issues, but after a few experiments I was able to capture what I really heard, I'll link the video bellow. The first part of the video shows the expected audio quality, the second part what I heard.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/XHe_zILpMZs\n\n- At 0:25 when the announcer said \"Combatant ready\", notice how the audio cuts off close to the end of the sentence, at this moment there were only two audio  sources playing and it already causes issues.\n\n- In game there are a dozen audio sources, here the issue is way more noticeable.\n\nI wasn't using Bluetooth, just a regular headphone with a headphone jack.\n\nEdit : Without headphones, I noticed a huge improvement in audio quality, the audio gets even better the moment I switch worlds, so during the screen fade out the audio quality gets crystal clear.",
